the target language is: prolog.

% A 'for all cases in which <C> it is the case that <D>' with no matching cases
% succeeds vacuously. This also exercises templates/facts whose names collide
% with Prolog built-ins (true/false): such facts are skipped rather than raising
% a "No permission to modify static procedure" error.

the templates are:
    true.
    false.
    test.

the knowledge base includes:

test if
    for all cases in which
        false
        it is the case that
        false.

scenario one is:
    true.
    one expects answers ["test"].

query one is:
    test.
